{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he took up his parable and said.</b> The parable is: From the top of the rocks I see him." "<b>From the hills of the east.</b> East." "<b>Come, curse me Jacob.</b> The word ואמר is lacking, and in the Song of Songs there are many like it, and it is a concise mode." "<b>Not numbered, Israel.</b> The sense is doubled, as is the way to express one meaning in variant words and repeat it for emphasis. And the word זועמה ought to have been on the pattern of זכרה, only since the ayin is opened because it is a guttural, there was between it and the zayin a cholam in place of a chatéf kamatz."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {3 "Ibn Ezra argues that זועמה should follow the pattern of זכרה; because the guttural ע takes a full vowel (pataḥ) rather than a reduced one, the preceding vowel is cholam instead of chatéf kamatz."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:07.108544599Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}